  "worked_solution": "Since the function is valid starting from $9$ A.M., we can conclude our interval is $[0,12].$\n\nApplying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12-0}{\\int }_{0}^{12}(50+14\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi t}{12}))\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{12}(50t-\\frac{168}{\\pi }\\,\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi t}{12}))|}_{0}^{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}[(50\\cdot 12-\\frac{168}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi \\cdot 12}{12}))-(50\\cdot 0-\\frac{168}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi \\cdot 0}{12}))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}[(600-\\frac{168}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\pi ))-(0-\\frac{168}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(0))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}[(600-\\frac{168}{\\pi }\\cdot (-1))-(-\\frac{168}{\\pi }\\cdot 1)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}[\\frac{600\\pi +168}{\\pi }+\\frac{168}{\\pi }] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}(\\frac{600\\pi +336}{\\pi }) \\\\  & =\\frac{600\\pi +336}{12\\pi } \\\\  & \u2248{58.9}^{\u2218}F.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
